{"name":"Lush Honeycomb","hex":"#fca81b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Juicy, succulent.","Mellow; soft;  easily turned; fertile."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A drunkard, sot, alcoholic.","Intoxicating liquor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lush"},{"term":"honeycomb","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substance made by bees (clade Anthophila) primarily from beeswax which has hexagonal cells to hold their larvae, and for storing pollen and honey to feed the larvae and themselves when other food is scarce; it is also eaten by humans as part of comb-honey;  a single sheet made up of two layers of this substance.","Something resembling honeycomb (noun sense 1) in having numerous cells or small holes."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To riddle (something) with small holes, especially in a pattern resembling a honeycomb (noun sense 1); also, to cause (something) to become hollow or weakened in this way.\n\nTo bore cavities or tunnels inside (something).","To riddle (something) with small holes, especially in a pattern resembling a honeycomb (noun sense 1); also, to cause (something) to become hollow or weakened in this way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honeycomb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Honeycomb","blocks":[{"text":"A honeycomb is a mass of hexagonal prismatic cells built from beeswax by honey bees in their nests to contain their brood and stores of honey and pollen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Honey_comb.jpg/330px-Honey_comb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeycomb","wikidata":"Q123339"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%287421128352%29.jpg/500px-Honeycombs_for_Sale_-_Saraeyn_-_Iranian_Azerbaijan_-_Iran_%28742